requirement.body:
#### Bug description

Generated MessagePackResolverGetFormatterHelper.GetFormatter() method contains an extra `;` after the switch statement, which is redundant. While no impact on compiled code, some tooling (like ReSharper) causes warnings about unreachable code (as the switch always returns).

#### Repro steps

Any code with a custom IMessagePackFormatter<> will result in the generated formatter with the extra semicolon in the generated file.

#### Expected behavior

No extra semicolon.

#### Actual behavior

The extra semicolon marked by HERE below.
```
	private static class MessagePackResolverGetFormatterHelper
	{
		private static readonly global::System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary<global::System.Type, int> closedTypeLookup = new global::System.Collections.Generic.Dictionary<global::System.Type, int>(2)
		{
			{ typeof(global::SomeTypeName), 0 },
			{ typeof(global::OtherTypeName), 1 },
		};

		internal static object GetFormatter(global::System.Type t)
		{
			if (closedTypeLookup.TryGetValue(t, out int closedKey))
			{
				switch (closedKey)
				{
					case 0: return new global::SomeTypeName();
					case 1: return new global::OtherTypeName();
					default: return null; // unreachable
				};       <---- HERE
			}

			return null;
		}
	}
```

- Version used: 3.1.4
- Runtime: .NET 8

#### Additional Context

I assume [this](https://github.com/MessagePack-CSharp/MessagePack-CSharp/blob/44aa149acce1de32881e007f53fad0f3db7dfdab/src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/Transforms/ResolverTemplate.tt#L75) and [this](https://github.com/MessagePack-CSharp/MessagePack-CSharp/blob/44aa149acce1de32881e007f53fad0f3db7dfdab/src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/Transforms/ResolverTemplate.tt#L88) line is causing the "problem".

